# Logic as engineering notation

A proposition is a statement that has a truth value. We will eventually use formal logic for proofs, specifications, invariants and reasoning about programs.

```math
{
  "label": "Implication",
  "tex": "P \\Rightarrow Q",
  "caption": "If P holds, Q must hold for the implication to be true in the intended proof step."
}
```

```quiz
{
  "id": "q-logic-01",
  "type": "single-choice",
  "prompt": "Which expression states that both P and Q hold?",
  "options": [
    {"id":"a","label":"P ∧ Q"},
    {"id":"b","label":"P ∨ Q"},
    {"id":"c","label":"¬P"}
  ],
  "answer": "a",
  "explanation": "The conjunction P ∧ Q is true exactly when both propositions are true."
}
```
